From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] musl: always use bundled regex (no REG_STARTEND in zig musl)

zig cc -target ARCH-linux-musl uses zig's bundled musl headers which may
not define REG_STARTEND. Rather than fighting the build system to pass
-DNO_REGEX into every compilation unit, define NO_REGEX directly at the
top of git-compat-util.h when targeting musl.

--- a/git-compat-util.h
+++ b/git-compat-util.h
@@ -1,3 +1,8 @@
+/* Use bundled regex on musl — zig cc's musl headers lack REG_STARTEND */
+#if defined(__musl__)
+# define NO_REGEX NeedsStartEnd
+# define REGEX_UNDEF_STARTEND
+#endif
+
 #ifndef GIT_COMPAT_UTIL_H
 #define GIT_COMPAT_UTIL_H
